{"units": [{"id": "kledouchos-def1", "translation": "priestess who keeps the keys"}, {"id": "kledouchos-quote1", "translation": "They say that Io once became the key-holder of Hera's house"}, {"id": "kledon-orth1", "translation": "omen"}, {"id": "kledon-def1", "translation": "omen"}, {"id": "kledon-def2", "translation": "clamor"}, {"id": "kledon-def3", "translation": "rumor"}, {"id": "kledon-def4", "translation": "fame, glory"}, {"id": "kledon-def5", "translation": "calling"}, {"id": "kledon-def6", "translation": "name"}, {"id": "kledon-quote1", "translation": "and I recognized for them omens hard to interpret"}, {"id": "kledon-quote2", "translation": "prayers and ancestral omens"}, {"id": "kledon-quote3", "translation": "hearing many hostile omens"}, {"id": "kledon-quote4", "translation": "because of such hostile omens"}, {"id": "kledon-quote5", "translation": "from an obscure omen"}, {"id": "kledon-quote6", "translation": "apart from foot-scrapers and the embroidered robes, a voice cries out"}, {"id": "kledon-quote7", "translation": "for children are saving omens for a man when he is dead"}, {"id": "kledon-quote8", "translation": "leaving these omens"}, {"id": "kledon-quote9", "translation": "I heard from afar the cry of an omen"}, {"id": "kledon-quote10", "translation": "I know the family and the omens that give it its name"}, {"id": "klezo-orth1", "translation": "to celebrate"}, {"id": "klezo-def1", "translation": "to celebrate"}, {"id": "klezo-quote1", "translation": "For was the report of him living or dead spread abroad by other sailors?"}, {"id": "klethron-orth1", "translation": "bar, bolt"}, {"id": "klethron-def1", "translation": "bar, bolt"}, {"id": "klethron-note1", "translation": "In the copies κλείθρων [of the bars]."}, {"id": "klethron-quote1", "translation": "when the bars were loosened"}, {"id": "klethron-word1", "translation": "of the bars"}, {"id": "kleroomai-orth1", "translation": "to cast lots"}, {"id": "kleroomai-def1", "translation": "to cast lots"}, {"id": "kleroomai-quote1", "translation": "and they left them casting lots"}, {"id": "kleros-orth1", "translation": "lot"}, {"id": "kleros-def1", "translation": "lot"}, {"id": "kleros-def2", "translation": "region, which fell to someone by lot"}, {"id": "kleros-note1", "translation": "unless these are the words of Archilochus."}, {"id": "kleros-quote1", "translation": "and a stranger distributes the lots"}, {"id": "kleros-quote2", "translation": "having obtained the land of Hellas by lot"}, {"id": "kleros-quote3", "translation": "according to the Ionian lot"}, {"id": "kleros-quote4", "translation": "holding all the lot of Cyprus and Paphos"}, {"id": "kles-orth1", "translation": "key"}, {"id": "kles-def1", "translation": "key"}, {"id": "kles-note1", "translation": "Concerning the duty of silence."}, {"id": "kles-quote1", "translation": "I alone of the gods know the keys of the house"}, {"id": "kles-quote2", "translation": "But there is also for me a key as guardian on my tongue"}, {"id": "kles-quote3", "translation": "for mortals upon whose tongue a golden key has come, the attendants of the Eumolpidae"}, {"id": "kleter-orth1", "translation": "summoner"}, {"id": "kleter-def1", "translation": "summoner"}, {"id": "kleter-quote1", "translation": "the summoner of the Erinys"}, {"id": "kleter-quote2", "translation": "he accomplished it without a summoner"}, {"id": "klyo-orth1", "translation": "to shut"}, {"id": "klyo-def1", "translation": "to shut"}, {"id": "klyo-quote1", "translation": "to shut the great Bosporus"}, {"id": "klyo-quote2", "translation": "a city shut in by the deep device of towers"}, {"id": "klimax-orth1", "translation": "ladder"}, {"id": "klimax-def1", "translation": "ladder"}, {"id": "klimax-quote1", "translation": "the ascents of a ladder"}, {"id": "klino-orth1", "translation": "to incline"}, {"id": "klino-def1", "translation": "to incline"}, {"id": "klino-quote1", "translation": "and the land of Asia has been brought to its knee"}, {"id": "klisia-orth1", "translation": "tent"}, {"id": "klisia-def1", "translation": "tent"}, {"id": "klisia-quote1", "translation": "inside the tent"}, {"id": "klonos-orth1", "translation": "tumult"}, {"id": "klonos-def1", "translation": "tumult"}, {"id": "klonos-quote1", "translation": "and horse-fighting tumults"}, {"id": "klonos-quote2", "translation": "shield-bearing tumults with spears"}, {"id": "klopaios-orth1", "translation": "stolen, furtive"}, {"id": "klopaios-def1", "translation": "stolen, furtive"}, {"id": "klopaios-quote1", "translation": "I hunt for the stolen source of fire"}, {"id": "klope-orth1", "translation": "theft"}, {"id": "klope-def1", "translation": "theft"}, {"id": "klope-quote1", "translation": "he disgraced the hospitable table by the thefts of a woman"}, {"id": "klope-quote2", "translation": "for having incurred the penalty of seizure and theft"}, {"id": "klydon-orth1", "translation": "wave, surge"}, {"id": "klydon-def1", "translation": "wave, surge"}, {"id": "klydon-quote1", "translation": "and the sea wave roars"}, {"id": "klydon-quote2", "translation": "when a wave of evils comes upon"}, {"id": "klydonion-orth1", "translation": "wave, surge"}, {"id": "klydonion-def1", "translation": "wave, surge"}, {"id": "klydonion-note1", "translation": "Thus I emended the reading interpolated in M: μελανόχρως [dark-skinned] (κελαινόχρως [dark-skinned] Pauw) δὲ πάλλεταί μου καρδία [and my heart is shaken]."}, {"id": "klydonion-quote1", "translation": "and the city in fair weather and in the surge did not receive the bilge with many blows"}, {"id": "klydonion-quote2", "translation": "and upon my heart stood a surge of bile"}, {"id": "klydonion-quote3", "translation": "and with dark-skinned surge the heart is shaken"}, {"id": "klydonion-word1", "translation": "dark-skinned (dark-skinned)"}, {"id": "klydonion-word2", "translation": "and my heart is shaken"}, {"id": "klyzo-orth1", "translation": "to boil up"}, {"id": "klyzo-def1", "translation": "to boil up"}, {"id": "klyzo-note1", "translation": "Improperly."}, {"id": "klyzo-quote1", "translation": "so that like a wave it boils up (thus Schuetz for κλύειν [to hear]) toward the light of this calamity much greater"}, {"id": "klytaimnestra-orth1", "translation": "Clytaemnestra"}, {"id": "klytaimnestra-def1", "translation": "Clytaemnestra, wife of Agamemnon, who comes on stage in the Agamemnon and Choephori, and the ghost of Clytaemnestra in the Eumenides"}, {"id": "klytaimnestra-quote1", "translation": "queen Clytaemnestra"}, {"id": "klytaimnestra-quote2", "translation": "honoring your power, Clytaemnestra"}, {"id": "klytaimnestra-quote3", "translation": "and it is fitting that these matters be a care to Clytaemnestra most of all in the house"}, {"id": "klytaimnestra-quote4", "translation": "where is Clytaemnestra?"}, {"id": "klytaimnestra-quote5", "translation": "for now I call you Clytaemnestra in a dream"}, {"id": "klytaimnestra-word1", "translation": "the ghost of Clytaemnestra"}, {"id": "klytos-orth1", "translation": "heard"}, {"id": "klytos-def1", "translation": "heard"}, {"id": "klytos-quote1", "translation": "in time the deep-minded Erinys heard"}, {"id": "klyo_v-orth1", "translation": "to obey"}, {"id": "klyo_v-def1", "translation": "to obey"}, {"id": "klyo_v-def2", "translation": "κλύω [to hear] with adjectives or adverbs is the same as 'I am called, I am named', in which sense the Latins also say audio [I hear]"}]}